{"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLTimeV6symbolAA0C6SymbolOSgvp","title":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"symbol","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTimeSymbol","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLTimeSymbolO"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"property"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTime"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTime\/symbol","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The symbol used to indicate common and cut time as well as a single number display."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"symbol","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTimeSymbol","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLTimeSymbolO","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTimeSymbol"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"symbol","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" attribute.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltime\/symbol"]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTime/symbol":{"title":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltime\/symbol","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The symbol used to indicate common and cut time as well as a single number display."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTime\/symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"symbol","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTimeSymbol","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLTimeSymbolO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTimeSymbol":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLTimeSymbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTimeSymbol","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltimesymbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTimeSymbol","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLTimeSymbol","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The time-symbol type indicates how to display a time signature. The normal value is the usual fractional"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"display, and is the implied symbol type if none is specified. Other options are the common and cut time"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"symbols, as well as a single number with an implied denominator. The note symbol indicates that the beat-type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"should be represented with the corresponding downstem note rather than a number. The dotted-note symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"indicates that the beat-type should be represented with a dotted downstem note that corresponds to three times"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the beat-type value, and a numerator that is one third the beats value."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTime":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTime","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTime"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltime","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTime"}],"title":"MXLTime","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Time signatures are represented by the beats element for the numerator and the beat-type element for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"denominator. The symbol attribute is used to indicate common and cut time symbols as well as a single number"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"display. Multiple pairs of beat and beat-type elements are used for composite time signatures with multiple"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"denominators, such as 2\/4 + 3\/8. A composite such as 3+2\/8 requires only one beat\/beat-type pair."}]}}}